<title>NETHERLANDS: BEGEMANN SELLS VEVEY UNIT TO WAGGONBAU.</title>
<headline>BEGEMANN SELLS VEVEY UNIT TO WAGGONBAU.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diversified industrial group Koninklijke Begemann Groep said on Monday it had signed a declaration of intent with Germany's Deutsche Waggonbau on the sale of its Vevey Technologies unit.</p>
<p>&quot;Deutsche Waggonbau Aktiengesellschaft will acquire 100 percent of the shares in Vevey Technologies SA Villeneuve&quot;, Begemann said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Begemann has holdings in some 40 industrial companies.</p>
<p>In September the company said it was unable to make a forecast of net profit for the whole of 1996 because of uncertainty about the level of results from the purchase or sale of holdings.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
